WEBVTT

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.710
A dinosaur!

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.040
No, she's not.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.710
I know! She's a snake!

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.900
This is Quetzalcoatl-san, the Antarctican.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.710
Antarctica?

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.040
Quetz... Quet... Que... Que...

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.300
Que-chan.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.900
I would rather you use my given 
name, Sassassul, please.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.720
Okay. Suu-chan, then.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.930
Pleased to meet you.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.400
Suu-chan-oneechan, open your mouth.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.840
Do it again.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.710
Girls! Don't be rude!

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.840
I'm sorry about my sisters.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.260
It's fine.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.720
It's much better for me if they 
approach without hesitation.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.730
Hello, Sue-chan.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.040
Well? She said hello to you.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.000
He... ll... o...

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.460
She's not like her big sis at all, huh?

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.570
The Chisters are just like her, though.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.040
Please don't do that. My neck will break.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:10.240
<i>When I was in my early 
elementary school years,</i>

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.390
<i>my nickname was "the doll," though...</i>

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.080
Nee-chan, we're all sweaty now.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.020
The sweat will wash off in the pool.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.080
Oh, yeah! The pool!

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:24.370
Hurry and come to the pool with us, 
Hime-neechan and everyone else!

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.980
No running!

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.130
I changed all by myself!

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.520
Good job.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.400
Yeah!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.450
We changed by ourselves, too!

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.540
That's not as hard for you three.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.220
Hmph!

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.810
Come on, let's go.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.740
You really don't have any.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:45.920
My kind don't need to nurse our young.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.830
Besides, I could say the 
same for you two...

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:52.570
We don't need to nurse young right now.

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.730
Nope, no need.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.510
It's deep in the middle, huh?

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:08.350
Here!

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.900
Hime-neetan, I can't swim here.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.750
That's true. Your feet touch the bottom.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.690
What's wrong?

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:25.810
Well...

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.040
I'm actually afraid of water.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:29.820
Huh?

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:32.210
When it's this shallow?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.510
The depth is not the issue.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:38.720
Being in water is what frightens me.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:43.980
In Antarctica, falling into 
the water means certain death.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.740
Don't you have hot springs and stuff?

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.530
Since we don't have sweat glands,

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.710
bathing is not a custom of our kind.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.260
We do clean our bodies, however.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.530
I'm impressed you made it across the ocean.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:01.240
Well, people who can't fly 
travel through the air, too.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.160
Come on, snake lady, hurry up!

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.500
Wh... I can't... Wait!

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.510
This way!

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.200
Are you dead?

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.240
I'm alive.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.520
Mew...

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.020
Are you okay?

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:23.690
Mew...

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.510
You're so cute!

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.330
Isn't she?

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:36.780
Well, we're gonna go swim 
in the racing pool for a bit.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.040
Coming, Hime?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.460
I'll stay here.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:40.820
Hime-neetan.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:42.830
I want to swim, too.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.040
Okay. Why don't we go together, then?

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:45.770
Yeah!

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.330
We're coming, too!

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:56.130
Hold it right there.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.440
What'd you do that for? Pervert!

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.760
I am not a pervert.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:03.080
You three can't go over there.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.850
But Shino-chan went!

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.260
She's a centaur.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.020
Besides, were you going
 to leave Sue-chan behind?

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.900
Hmph!

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:14.560
If you keep making that face,
 it'll get stuck that way.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.530
I don't want it to get stuck like this!

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.520
If you want to swim, I'll teach you here.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:21.530
I'll be here, too.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:32.280
They're really good swimmers.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.880
I'm surprised by Kyo-chan...

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.110
A mermaid! Wasn't that amazing?

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.170
Oh, it's deep...

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.690
Because there are diving 
boards over there, I guess.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:50.270
Can we go to the other end?

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:53.590
My feet don't touch the 
bottom past this spot.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.430
You can't swim, Nee-tan?

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:57.390
No, it's not that...

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:00.620
But if I go under, 
no one will be able to help me.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:07.930
Come to think of it, 
how do merfolk climb up to the poolside?

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:10.500
They probably have a friend pull them up.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.740
That was some leap.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.690
It looked like everyone was more 
interested in her chest to me.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:35.750
Your feet will touch the bottom soon,

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:38.900
so stretch your front legs forward 
and just kick with your back legs.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.320
Otherwise, you might crack a hoof.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.300
Okay, we're here.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.390
I'm pretty tired, so let's head 
back to where the Chi-chans are.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:49.030
Okay.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.440
Practicing swimming?

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:58.480
Meow.

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:01.040
Chi-chans, let's play!

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:05.420
Hmph. You can just go 
play in the deep pool.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:06.220
Hey!

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.070
Chi-chan!

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.110
What was that for?

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:16.240
What do you think you're doing?!

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:18.440
Take that!

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:19.530
Meow!

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.090
<b>Concessions</b>

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.090
<b>Hot Cocoa</b>

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:38.700
That's hot, so blow on it first.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.410
Like it?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.040
Uh-huh!

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.520
That warms me up.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.700
Pools do chill the body.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:48.150
Uh-oh.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.470
Sleepy, Sue-chan?

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.120
She did lots of playing today.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:00.070
Are you sleepy too, Shino-chan? 
I can't blame you.

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:04.750
That won't work for you three.

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:06.330
Why not?!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.560
There's only one of me.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.180
I can't carry all of you home.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.740
But Shino-chan has one 
nee-chan all for herself!

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:17.000
Why is there only one of you?

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.050
It's all totally unfair!

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.310
You three...

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:24.150
If you had three big sisters, 
you'd have three times the nagging, too.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:26.000
That would be bad.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:30.980
Well, today's special, 
so you can go ahead and sleep.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.150
Wait, don't just...

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:37.010
You have three extra big 
sisters today, after all.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:39.550
Yay! Carry me, too!

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.170
I don't see why not.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:45.020
I used to help care for 
my younger sister, too.

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:48.100
Suu-chan, you have a younger sister?

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:52.750
Yes. We were all born from the same queen.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:57.480
That means all of us are sisters by blood.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.210
That's really wild...

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:12.730
<b>Shaved Ice now on sale!!</b>

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:02.160
But when I speak of my "younger sister,"

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.720
I refer to a specific child
 I was responsible for raising.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:10.380
It's essentially the same as your concept 
of a younger sister, I believe.

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:20.290
Are you sure? 
Our house is still pretty far.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:23.790
Well, a day like this isn't 
so bad, every now and then.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:28.280
By the way, you mentioned that you 
raised your younger sister...

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.910
I'm getting a little sleepy, too.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:35.620
We can't carry you, you know.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:36.840
Aw...

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.930
Hey, don't drop Shino-chan.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:41.930
I know...

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:46.930
<b>First Experiences Are Scary and Fun 
All in One... Pardon the Rhyme.</b>

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:51.940
<b>Occult Movies You Watch as 
a Kid Are 140% Scarier.</b>

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.520
<b>Earth Sciences Prep Room</b>

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.400
I'd like to tell some scary stories.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:07.330
Scary stories? The kind 
with ghosts and stuff?

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.200
Yep.

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:11.220
Boo.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:12.630
Eek!

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.360
Cut that out!

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.750
Scary stories in broad daylight?

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:20.510
No, we're going to tell them at night.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.290
I was thinking this Friday.

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:24.920
If that works for you guys, 
I'll get permission.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.660
To stay overnight?

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.350
I expect to wrap up by about 10:00.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:35.410
Are you even allowed to decide
 that without your tiny president?

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:37.660
See, that's the whole point!

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.690
You're awfully impertinent 
for underclassmen, aren't you?

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.790
Are we?

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:44.940
I don't think so.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:48.570
I need to get all of you
 to commit your schedules first.

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:51.910
I can't have you all backing out 
after I invite Towako-chan.

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:55.440
Anyway, if you want to tell scary stories,

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:58.150
why not just do it with Mystery 
Spot-senpai over there?

00:12:58.150 --> 00:13:00.540
There's a point to getting 
Towako-chan to come.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.890
I see. So that's it.

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:05.210
Yes, that's it.

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:07.720
You actually said it...

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:11.970
She won't come if it's just 
the two of us, you know?

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:15.420
But despite how she acts, 
she gets lonely easily,

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.870
so if you'll all be there, 
I'm sure she'll come.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:21.990
Not to mention, we can all get to know our 
clubmates better. Two birds with one stone!

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:23.970
What the heck?

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:25.690
So we're only a pretext?

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:26.490
Why not?

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.990
<b>Shinkanata High School 
Occult Science Club 
100 Scary Stories</b>

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:29.530
We can compile all our 
stories into a booklet

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.990
and submit it as a record of our 
activities at the end of the year.

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:38.060
That'll guarantee us a club room and a budget
 for next year. Three birds with one stone!

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:41.010
Uh, we never said we wanted 
to stay in this club.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:44.250
Well, it might be nice to have 
a place to hang out, though.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:47.750
But still...

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:51.850
I have to teach brats karate, shower, 
and then come back to school?

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.010
We should support them, though!

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:55.690
What?

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:58.610
I mean... why not?

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:00.000
Kimihara-kun...

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.890
Thank you!

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.780
What are you doing?! Okay, 
forget we ever discussed this!

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:13.410
I just expressed my happiness 
a little too eagerly.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.530
I wonder about that...

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:16.910
It's true.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:18.850
I'll hug you, too.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:20.940
You're gonna sexually harass me as well?

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:24.920
Anyway, Senpai, can't you just 
ask her on a date like normal?

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:29.020
If that would work, 
I wouldn't ask you guys for help.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:33.730
Yeah, but scary stories?
 Don't you have any other ideas?

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:37.340
A tour of mystery spots, 
a power spot pilgrimage,

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:38.740
a UFO-summoning party...

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.530
At least make it a horror movie night.

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:44.220
So you want to get closer
 to the club president, then?

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:44.870
Yep!

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:46.850
So please!

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:47.640
Sure!

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:52.190
You sure you can handle scary stories?

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:53.690
I'll do my best!

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.550
So I can count all of you in, right?

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:57.920
Fine with me, I guess.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.980
Well, if Hime's going...

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:01.520
I will if you all do.

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:04.930
Gladly. It sounds like a valuable 
opportunity to experience your culture.

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:09.210
Great! Okay, each of you come up 
with about ten scary stories!

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:10.780
That many?

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:13.320
I'm kind of excited 
to hear everyone's stories!

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.770
You're not scared?

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:17.220
As long as there are no ghosts...

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.540
We're all set!

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:21.440
But Senpai, do you think 
it'll work that well?

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:25.210
Shrimp-senpai doesn't seem like she'd 
be bothered by scary stories.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.980
This might not turn out like you expect.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:30.850
I only believe what I can verify as truth!

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.940
You don't know anything about Towako.

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:36.800
I know all about her, 
including her measurements.

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:38.460
I like my chances.

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:39.440
Hey, come on.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:50.410
The school is kind of scary at night...

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:51.420
Yeah, kind of.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:55.290
What? Didn't you say you 
don't believe in ghosts?

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.420
It's scary whether you 
believe in them or not!

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:03.310
I heard this was a graveyard before 
they built the school here.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:07.100
Just kidding. It used to be a field.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.180
Jeez, don't do that!

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:14.610
You hear a lot of rumors in a city full
 of research schools like this, though.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:17.700
I heard the story about the
human-faced dog originated here.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:22.360
I also heard it was a hidden village for 
victims of abandoned human experimentation.

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:24.710
No! That's scary!

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:27.450
More of those silly urban legends?

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:30.450
Also, you two, don't start 
before we're ready.

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:34.050
A Japanese-style room?

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.910
This building must have had 
a different purpose originally.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.110
Candles?

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.780
I figured we should go all-out.

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:44.460
I'm not sticking around 
for one hundred scary stories.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:47.220
It's just about getting into the mood.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.670
I'm already scared!

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:52.570
All right, let's begin.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.090
Okay, I'll start.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.880
We all know that this town

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:05.370
started as a college and
industrial research center, right?

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:11.280
This story takes place just 
after the town was founded...

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:20.190
And that experimental subject 
still lurks in the sewers,

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:23.810
waiting for the next unfortunate 
victim to come along.

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:28.080
Next will be... you!

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:32.870
Don't laugh! Want to trade seats with me?

00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:34.560
Nah, I'll pass.

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:37.030
What's so scary about 
an urban legend like that?

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:40.920
Well, it seems like something 
like that could really be out there...

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:43.030
The fact that it was a story
about genetic manipulation

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:47.030
instead of fallen samurai or yokai made 
it fitting for a school town like this.

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:50.490
They say that any sufficiently advanced
technology is indistinguishable from magic,

00:17:50.490 --> 00:17:54.100
but the fact that you don't know 
how far you can take it, or how,

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:55.980
is the true essence of the story.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:18:00.590
You mean that we don't know 
the limits of science?

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:03.010
Yeah, that's right.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:05.480
Don't you have scary stories in Antarctica?

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:10.690
No. We don't believe in souls 
or supernatural phenomena.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.330
Or I should say, we can't
conceive of such things.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:18.810
Of course, I don't mean 
to deny your beliefs!

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:21.620
Nah, we don't really believe 
in that stuff, either.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.120
Well, it scares me!

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:27.200
But speaking of mysteries, 
when I was young,

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:30.870
I chose to walk on the cracks 
of flagstone streets.

00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:40.550
When the one in charge of raising me 
asked about my reason for doing so...

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:49.610
A pitfall?

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:53.920
Yes. When I think about it now,
 I know no such thing exists, but...

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:55.830
So it's kind of like this?

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:59.660
Even Antarcticans can 
believe in superstitions,

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:01.620
but they deny the very fact

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.950
that a culture that emphasizes reason
and logic can believe in superstitions.

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:11.530
That's wonderful! Coming to the 
human world was worth it!

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:13.870
Uh, no, I don't even know if I'm right...

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:16.070
We used to do something like that, though.

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:19.700
Like when we only walked on
 the white lines in crosswalks.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:21.250
Oh, yeah, we did!

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:25.050
And only walking in shadows 
when going home from school.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:28.340
And if you stepped in the wrong spot,
 you'd fall into an abyss.

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:29.730
Hey!

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.390
We're getting off 
the subject of scary stories!

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:35.590
But science is more interesting 
than occult stuff.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:39.640
You say that, 
but I bet you're actually scared.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:40.820
Hmph!

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:42.840
Oops...

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:47.820
Okay, let's get back on track 
with a scientific one.

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:52.420
Lots of people say they've seen spirits.

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:57.500
For example, soldiers say they've seen Warring
States commanders or World War soldiers,

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:02.280
but they never see Kofun Period 
armor or Bakumatsu rifles.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:04.460
No primitive men in furs, either.

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:08.470
And if there are animal spirits,

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:10.810
they're always things like 
dogs, cats, foxes, or tanuki.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:13.140
All animals that exist closely with humans.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:15.500
No one sees Naumann's elephants.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:20.010
In other words, no one witnesses things 
that don't exist in their own consciousness.

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:22.550
That's why they're regarded 
as hallucinations.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:28.680
But I have a friend who was walking 
by the sea in a certain town,

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.930
when he saw...

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:46.050
Anomalocaris?

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:47.710
Aren't those extinct?

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.780
And how is it walking?

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:01.170
"A predatory creature from 
the Cambrian Period.

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:04.080
It's believed that they 
swam in shallow seas,

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:07.250
but fossils have been found that had legs."

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:11.630
No way... Some of them could walk?!

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:16.710
My friend saw something that didn't 
exist in his own consciousness.

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.830
So it had to be...

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:29.930
the ghost of an Anomalocaris!

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:39.440
You're just trying 
to scare us with your face.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.910
Oh, please. I can't put up with this.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:45.570
I'm going to the restroom.

00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:47.900
Anyone want to go with me?

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:55.080
Don't get me wrong! I'm not scared, okay?!

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:56.540
I'll go with you.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:57.470
Me, too.

00:21:57.470 --> 00:22:00.910
Seriously, I'm <i>not</i> scared! Ugh!

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
